meta {
  name: 02 Update Status
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/delta-checks/{{deltaCheckId}}/status
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "status": "UNDER_REVIEW",
    "notes": "Reviewed against clinical history — consistent with known condition."
  }
}

docs {
  Manual status update (LABORATORY.docx §8.4): Delta Check shares the
  review-workflow vocabulary (`AlertReviewStatus`) with Critical Alerts and Out
  of Range: `status` one of `NEW` | `ACKNOWLEDGED` | `UNDER_REVIEW` |
  `INITIATE_RERUN` | `IN_PROGRESS` | `RERUN_COMPLETED` | `ACCEPT_AND_RELEASE` |
  `RESOLVED`. New items await review; after review the technician either sends
  the result for re-run (`INITIATE_RERUN` → `IN_PROGRESS` → `RERUN_COMPLETED`)
  or accepts without re-run (`ACCEPT_AND_RELEASE`); `RESOLVED` once released.
  `notes` optional.

  404 `DELTA_CHECK_NOT_FOUND`.
}
